<%# locals: () %>
<%# How much is in the list: "n Zeiten · HH:MM" (Handout §4).

    ⚠️ Its own id, because it must be able to ARRIVE ON ITS OWN. It sits above
    time_sessions_list_frame and is a reading of the very query that frame
    answers, so a search would narrow the list underneath and leave this figure
    standing. One of TimeSessionsHelper::FRAME_DEPENDENT_REGIONS; _index_table
    streams every one of them back with a frame answer.

    In the face the LIST uses for its figures: a reader compares this against the
    durations underneath, and tabular-nums keeps it from jittering as the count
    changes.

    Only the count and the sum. No subject count: that belongs to the group
    headers, where a reader can see which subjects they are. And the count is of
    BOOKINGS -- pagy.count is rows, one subject in one month. %>
<%# Same rule as its neighbours: no figure, no region. create.turbo_stream
    renders this table with no filtered totals at all. %>
<% return if @total_filtered_count.nil? %>
<span id="time_result_summary" class="font-mono tabular-nums text-[15px] font-semibold text-cream-900" data-result-summary>
  <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index.result_summary',
        count: t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index.result_times', count: @total_filtered_count.to_i),
        duration: TimeSession.format_duration(@total_filtered_duration.to_i)) %>
</span>
